node_modules/
dist/
# The AssessHub build (npm run build:hub): served by AssessHub at /scope/, regenerated, never authored.
dist-hub/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Review artefacts are REGENERATED, never authored: capture.mjs rebuilds shots/, blind-pair.mjs
# rebuilds blind/, measure-inp.mjs rebuilds reports/. Committing them would put megabytes of
# third-party product screenshots into the history and make every visual change a binary diff.
# The scripts that produce them ARE tracked, which is what makes the review reproducible.
review/shots/
review/blind/
review/reports/

# Scratch written by review and audit agents while they work. Untracked AND ignored is the
# difference between "not part of the tree" and "about to be swept into a `git add -A`": .audit/
# held 20+ probe scripts and a shots/ folder during this build with nothing declaring them
# disposable. src/core/source-hygiene.test.ts skips ignored directories for the same reason.
#
# THE CLASS, NOT THE ONE DIRECTORY NAME. The rule above was written for `.audit/` and applied to
# `.audit/` — and the agents then wrote their scratch somewhere else. Measured 2026-09-21:
# `.probe/` (18 .mjs plus a shots/ tree), 93 `review/_audit_*.mjs`, 2 `review/_repair_*.mjs` and
# seven loose files at the repository root were all untracked AND unignored, so the first
# `git add -A` would have swept roughly a hundred probe scripts and 600 KB of probe PNGs into the
# first commit. A remedy aimed at a directory NAME instead of at the class it means is the exact
# defect shape this repository documents elsewhere, committed by its own ignore file.
#
# So the class is named by what these files ARE — an agent wrote it to look at something — using
# the prefixes the agents actually use, at any depth, plus the directories and the generated
# tool output. Preferred convention remains: put probes under `.audit/`. These patterns are the
# backstop for when that is forgotten, not a licence to skip it.
#
# NOTE this does NOT weaken `src/core/source-hygiene.test.ts`. Its walk skips a fixed list of
# DIRECTORIES, not gitignored paths, so a probe dropped in `src/` is still walked, still collected
# by the test glob, and still caught by its structural zero-assertion gate — which is what caught
# `src/_audit_honesty.test.ts`. Ignoring stops a probe being COMMITTED; that gate stops it RUNNING.
.audit/
shots/
_audit_*
_repair_*
_probe_*
.probe/
#
# The prefix list above was STILL a named subset. Measured after it landed: the baseline commit
# 857b520 swept in `review/_fix_*.mjs` (4) and `review/_fixshots/` (16 PNGs), and a later agent
# wrote `review/_verify_cluster_claims.mjs` — two prefixes no list had named. In `review/` the
# convention every agent actually follows is the leading underscore, and no authored harness
# (capture.mjs, blind-pair.mjs, measure-*.mjs, layout-guard.mjs, REFERENCES.md, ...) uses one,
# so the class is the underscore itself. NB: ignoring does not untrack; the 20 files already in
# 857b520 need `git rm -r --cached review/_fix_*.mjs review/_fixshots` in a deliberate commit.
review/_*
# 2026-09-22: 175 accumulated review/_* entries and the root-level d4/d7 dumps were MOVED (not
# deleted — several are cited as measurement provenance in source comments) into ONE directory,
# `review/_scratch/` (root dumps under `review/_scratch/root/`). New scratch goes there; do not add
# another ignore pattern for a new prefix.

# Playwright's own output directory, and the criterion-indexed dumps audit runs leave at the root
# (`d4_contrast.json`, `d7_reduce.png`, `d7_report.json` — named for the acceptance criterion the
# run was measuring). Generated, per-run, and never read twice.
test-results/
/d[0-9]_*.json
/d[0-9]_*.png

# A snapshot other than the tracked sample compiles here (tools/compile-all.mjs --source <file>). It is
# the place a REAL assessment's compiled model lands — client hostnames, addresses, serials — so it is
# ignored, and it is the ONLY place inside the repository compile-all will write such a compile: every
# other in-repository --out (src/, dist/ — served at /scope and bundled — public/, review/, node_modules/,
# Git-ignored or not) is refused, and so is this directory itself if this line is ever removed.
.local-data/
